WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.288
When routing tables determine which routes are the best routes, the routing protocols used,

00:05.288 --> 00:11.290
as we have seen with RIP and OSPF, help determine which routes are considered to be the best routes.

00:11.290 --> 00:23.130
All other things being equal, however, a big determining factor in routes is one column we see here, the metric column. Basically, the lower the metric, the better the route.

00:23.130 --> 00:32.844
Factors that determine the metric include: directly connected routers, which will have a very low metric, static routes will also have a low metric,

00:32.844 --> 00:41.271
like this one here, and then after that, the routing protocol being used and the mechanisms it uses will determine the metric.

00:41.271 --> 00:49.090
For the exam, keep in mind the importance of the metric number in determining best routes for a routing table.

